{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaZxatfzKZADXf4LST9L","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Why:** The printable visit summary is guarded by the privilege `App: Can generate a Visit Summary`. The constant is defined in `PatientDocumentsPrivilegeConstants` and checked in `VisitSummaryPdfReport.generatePdf` (`openmrs-module-patientdocuments/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/patientdocuments/common/PatientDocumentsPrivilegeConstants.java:18`, `openmrs-module-patientdocuments/api/src/main/java/org/openmrs/module/patientdocuments/reports/VisitSummaryPdfReport.java:88-89`). The module's `config.xml` never declared that privilege, so OpenMRS had no privilege record to assign to a role. Only superusers, who hold every privilege, could pass `Context.requirePrivilege`. The check was introduced in commit a7e0bfb (O3-5668, PR #16), which added the constant and the check but not the declaration.

**Fix:** Commit `9fc46c2cf8f6b7d3f2758379ac9b7af2d848b22a`, "Declare Visit Summary privilege in config.xml (#31)", added the `<privilege>` block for `App: Can generate a Visit Summary` to `config.xml` (diff verified: lines 55-58 added). The commit message names no ticket, and the Falkon data I can reach has none linked, so I can't give a ticket key for it.

**Other findings:**
- The fix is in the commit listed above, not in the later O3-5678 commit (`fc5dbea`), which only touched paper-size handling.
- The preview's `generateSamplePdf` uses `GET_GLOBAL_PROPERTIES`, not this privilege, by design (`VisitSummaryPdfReport.java:108-111`). That is unrelated to the bug.

